At128/8 and one epoch/accumulation1, each iteration must execute16 optimizer steps **per rank** on the synchronized model,16,384 global game transitions and32,768 learner-seat turns. Two iterations=32 optimizer steps/rank,32,768 game transitions. Native_threads1 keeps CPU use bounded; measurement for production choice remains separate. Tiny model/short episode explicitly change workload; these numbers are denominators, not a speed claim. If smoke is later upgraded to production model/compile/FlashAttention, freeze this result separately; Phase 6.1 teacher+dense-memory qualification still follows Phase 6.0 flash verification.

**Discriminating observations:** finite policy/value/entropy/loss/grad metrics; exactly16 optimizer steps/iteration; rank seed sets disjoint through construction/autoresets; the pod DMA fence test (Task C) passes and no Task 3.6 first-minibatch alarm fires (current0.05 threshold, not proof of all buffer integrity); terminal records with raw-bank winners, int episode_steps32 and32-counter metrics; no stale reset-bank outcome; completed transition/game/learner-seat denominators; correct W&B run/project/status. Add an isolated intentional-failure run bounded to one pre-update failure to verify L7 reports failed/crashed rather than finished; telemetry unavailability remains visible and makes that check inconclusive, not successful.

