docs/model-architecture.md:780:- **Startup workload check** (`python/owl/model/kaggriculture_workload.py`, Task 3.4): `ppo_forward_workloads` derives the per-rank seat rows of every PPO forward from config shapes (rollout `n_envs × 2`, minibatch `spm × horizon × 2`, teacher chunk `min(teacher_spm, n_envs) × horizon × 2` when `teacher_mode` is set, evaluation `n_envs × 2`; a BC caller adds its own `ForwardWorkload`). `check_workload_headroom` divides them by the model's own `rows_per_chunk` at the full padded sequence length and by `head_rows_per_chunk`, and raises when one row cannot fit either limit or a workload is empty. Head calls are exact; trunk calls are a full-padding **upper bound** and trunk headroom a **lower bound**, because the packed path plans chunks from actual token counts (16,384 rows of 300 tokens need 2 packed chunks, not 3). `scripts/run_ppo.py` runs the check through `_check_model_workload` after the per-rank shapes are final (runtime-GPU adaptation included) and before the run directory, env or model exist, and prints one headroom line per workload on the main process; Orbit models do not chunk and are skipped. At `configs/kaggriculture_2rank.yaml` the teacher chunk runs as at most 3 trunk and exactly 2 head calls; at 4 ranks, at most 2 and 1. The configs load through the real `FullConfig.from_file`, and the startup tests drive `main` from those YAML files (fresh, CLI override and resume paths). After the check, an explicit Kaggriculture guard keeps the launch stopped before the run directory exists: the native environment is available, but Task 3.1 rollout storage and action mapping still require Orbit batches.
